<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                    xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=System.Runtime">

    <!-- Design tokens: typography.
         Font: Vazirmatn (OFL, bundled as an embedded asset — no runtime CDN),
         matching the reference (Animora-UI) which imports Vazirmatn.

         IMPORTANT: Vazirmatn is bundled as the six OFFICIAL upstream STATIC
         weight files (Regular/Medium/SemiBold/Bold/ExtraBold/Black — see
         scripts/build_vazirmatn_weights.py). THREE earlier attempts failed:
           1. Upstream VARIABLE font — Avalonia can't weight-resolve it, so every
              non-Regular label rendered as solid black boxes.
           2. Static weights with each heavy file keeping its OWN legacy family
              name + leftover variable STAT/fvar tables — matcher couldn't
              collapse them into one family; heavy weights fell back to .notdef.
           3. Forcing ALL six files to ID1="Vazirmatn" with a legacy RIBBI
              subfamily of only "Regular"/"Bold". That collided three files onto
              (Vazirmatn, Regular) and three onto (Vazirmatn, Bold). The RIBBI
              model allows ONE face per (family, subfamily): Linux/FreeType kept
              all six (so the sandbox looked fixed) but Windows DirectWrite kept
              only one Bold + one Regular and discarded Medium/SemiBold/ExtraBold/
              Black — so ExtraBold headings were black boxes ON WINDOWS ONLY.
         Current fix: use the upstream static faces verbatim. They use the correct
         cross-platform layout — RIBBI base pair (ID1="Vazirmatn" + ID2 Regular/
         Bold) for 400/700, and a UNIQUE legacy family ("Vazirmatn Medium",
         "Vazirmatn SemiBold", "Vazirmatn ExtraBold", "Vazirmatn Black") plus
         preferred family ID16="Vazirmatn" for the other weights. No legacy
         collision, no variable tables, so Windows/macOS/Linux all resolve each
         FontWeight (400..900) to real outlines. The avares:// URI below matches
         on the preferred family "Vazirmatn" and exposes all six weights.
         NEVER re-collapse the heavy weights back onto ID1="Vazirmatn" — that is
         attempt #3, which silently passes on Linux and breaks Windows.

         Type scale + the weight tokens below mirror the reference's observed
         heading/body sizes and weights (400/500/600/700/800) so all app text is
         standardized to one font and one consistent weight ramp. -->

    <FontFamily x:Key="AppFontFamily">avares://Animora.Desktop/Assets/Fonts#Vazirmatn</FontFamily>

    <sys:Double x:Key="FontSizeXs">11</sys:Double>
    <sys:Double x:Key="FontSizeSm">13</sys:Double>
    <sys:Double x:Key="FontSizeMd">15</sys:Double>
    <sys:Double x:Key="FontSizeLg">19</sys:Double>
    <sys:Double x:Key="FontSizeXl">26</sys:Double>

    <!-- Weight tokens: bundled Vazirmatn static weights. Reference maps:
         body=400/500, labels/emphasis=600, headings/values=700, hero=800. -->
    <FontWeight x:Key="FontWeightRegular">Normal</FontWeight>
    <FontWeight x:Key="FontWeightMedium">Medium</FontWeight>
    <FontWeight x:Key="FontWeightSemiBold">SemiBold</FontWeight>
    <FontWeight x:Key="FontWeightBold">Bold</FontWeight>
    <FontWeight x:Key="FontWeightExtraBold">ExtraBold</FontWeight>

</ResourceDictionary>
